RM(1)                          P32W Unix                           RM(1)

NAME
       rm - remove files

SYNOPSIS
       rm [-fir] [--] name ...

DESCRIPTION
       rm removes the directory entry of each name. The file itself
       goes when its last link is gone and no process has it open.
       Removing an entry needs write permission on the directory,
       not on the file; rm does not ask about files you cannot
       write. In a sticky directory such as /tmp (mode 1777) only
       the file's owner (or root) may remove it.

       A directory is refused (rm: dir is a directory) unless -r is
       given, and . and .. (as the last component of a name) are
       always refused. An error with one name is reported and rm
       goes on with the next.

OPTIONS
       -f     say nothing about names that do not exist; with no
              names at all, exit quietly with status 0. Cancels -i.
       -i     ask before removing each file, on the error output
              ("rm: remove x? "); a line that starts with y or Y
              is yes. With -r a directory is asked about once,
              before what is in it. Cancels -f.
       -r, -R remove directories recursively: everything in them,
              then the directory itself. Paths longer than 255
              characters are reported (name too long) and left.
       --     ends the options, for names that start with -.

       Options may be combined (-rf) or given separately; they
       must come before the names. Of -f and -i the last wins.

EXAMPLES
       rm a.out *.o
       rm -r /mnt/backup/old
       rm -- -junk                a name that starts with -

EXIT STATUS
       0 if everything was removed (or declined with -i); 1 if
       something could not be (rm: name: and the reason); 2 for a
       usage error: an unknown option, or no name without -f.

SEE ALSO
       rmdir(1), ln(1), mv(1), unlink(2), rmdir(2)

BUGS
       -f hides only "does not exist": other errors are still
       reported. A directory that -r could not empty is left, and
       its contents that could not be removed are reported.
